    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418-a1">

                <pb facs="0591" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harmon to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington,
                                D. C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Further answering your communication of
                    November 14, concerning the habeas corpus cases in the western district of
                    Texas, I have the honor to say that these cases having been decided December 27,
                    1894, the time to appeal has already expired under the provisions of the act of
                    March 3, 1893, chapter 226. For this reason an appeal can not be directed. I am
                    informed by the district attorney that the marshal was not requested to join in
                    the appeal.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Judson Harmon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Attorney-General.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
